meta {
  name: Create Product Attribute
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-attributes
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "wc_test_text",
    "type": "TextAttribute"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.data.type: eq TextAttribute
}

docs {
  `POST /api/v3/product-attributes` -- creates a product attribute of the
  specified type.

  Confirmed live 2026-09-07/08 against "David's Dev Account". All tested types
  returned `201 Created`.

  ## Fixture
  `TextAttribute` "wc_test_text" kept -- id `6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e1`, for
  Products (Phase 2b) to reference in its `attributes` map.

  ## Label defaulting
  `label` defaults to the same value as `name` when omitted. Must match the
  `^[a-z0-9_]+$` pattern the spec declares for `label`, so `name` values that
  are already lowercase/underscore-safe work as a default label for free.

  ## group_ids linkage -- open item
  `group_ids: ["6a9f1b872b6fd055ffb7c7df"]` is accepted without error on create,
  but is **not** reflected back in either the create response or a subsequent
  `GET`/`_fields=group_ids`. Inconclusive whether the group linkage actually
  persists -- worth re-checking from the attribute-group side in a later session.

  ## Not idempotent to re-run
  Re-running once the fixture exists returns `409 Conflict`
  `{"errors":[{"name":"AlreadyExists","description":"An attribute with the same
  name already exists"}]}` -- same status as attribute groups (not categories'
  `422`).

  ## GET /product-attributes listing -- CROSS-TENANT DATA LEAK (confirmed bug)
  `GET /product-attributes` returns attributes from **other accounts**, not just
  the authenticated account. This is a confirmed, reproducible data-isolation bug.
  The listing endpoint must NOT be used in customer-facing workflows until Plytix
  resolves it. Use `GET /product-attributes/{id}` (by known ObjectId) instead.
  Flag to Plytix as a live security/privacy bug requiring immediate attention.
  **Re-tested 2026-09-21**: still returning cross-tenant attribute records
  (`account_id` values `5d0bae46c7ab750468a3d67e`, `60795dcd302a91ac42e7f5f9`).
  Not fixed.

  ## Supported attribute types (15 total, one undocumented)
  `openapi_pimv3.json`'s `POST /product-attributes` `oneOf` declares 14 types.
  The live API's pydantic validator recognizes **15** -- including
  `HierarchyAttribute`, which is absent from the spec. All 9 "standard" types
  below were smoke-tested successfully with minimal `{name, type}` bodies (plus
  `options` for multi-select types):

  | Type | Notes |
  |---|---|
  | `TextAttribute` | Fixture kept (`wc_test_text`, id `6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e1`) |
  | `MultilineAttribute` | No extra required fields |
  | `BooleanAttribute` | No extra required fields |
  | `DateAttribute` | `include_time` defaults `false` |
  | `DecimalAttribute` | No extra required fields |
  | `HtmlAttribute` | No extra required fields |
  | `IntAttribute` | No extra required fields |
  | `MediaGalleryAttribute` | No extra required fields |
  | `UrlAttribute` | No extra required fields |
  | `DropdownAttribute` | `options` array required; `manual_sorting`/`sort_ascending`/`restricted` get real server-side defaults (`true`, `true`, `false`) |
  | `MultiSelectAttribute` | Same defaulting as `DropdownAttribute` |
  | `MediaAttribute` | No extra required fields |
  | `FormulaAttribute` | `formula_str` required; **account limit**: Dev account capped at 2 -- create path unconfirmed on a fresh account (only limit-enforcement 422 confirmed) |
  | `CompletenessAttribute` | `attributes: []` works; `attributes: [{id: "..."}]` with real references **500s** (confirmed bug -- see example below) |
  | `HierarchyAttribute` | Passes pydantic validation but **500s** on create -- unfinished/unexposed feature, not documentation-ready |

  ## Re-test 2026-09-21 — both 500s persist
  Re-tested `HierarchyAttribute` and `CompletenessAttribute`-with-real-refs against
  the live API. Both still return `500 ConfigurationError`. Neither has been fixed
  in the ~2 weeks since initial discovery. Flag to Plytix for resolution before
  either type appears in customer-facing documentation.

  ## _fields ignored on GET-by-id (new finding)
  `GET /product-attributes/{id}?_fields=id` still returns the **full** shape.
  `_fields` only applies to list/search endpoints, never to single-resource
  `GET /{resource}/{id}` -- generalizes Phase 0's finding.
}

example {
  name: Create TextAttribute - Success (201)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-07. Minimal body; label defaults to name value. Fixture wc_test_text kept as Phase 2b dependency.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-attributes
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "name": "wc_test_text",
        "type": "TextAttribute"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 201
      text: Created
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "id": "6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e1",
            "name": "wc_test_text",
            "label": "wc_test_text",
            "description": null,
            "status": "ACTIVE",
            "type": "TextAttribute"
          },
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: Create DropdownAttribute - Success (201, with options)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-07. options array required; boolean fields (manual_sorting, sort_ascending, restricted) receive real server-side defaults rather than being left null.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-attributes
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "name": "wc_test_dropdown",
        "type": "DropdownAttribute",
        "options": ["Small", "Medium", "Large"]
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 201
      text: Created
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "id": "6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e3",
            "name": "wc_test_dropdown",
            "label": "wc_test_dropdown",
            "description": null,
            "status": "ACTIVE",
            "type": "DropdownAttribute",
            "options": ["Small", "Medium", "Large"],
            "manual_sorting": true,
            "sort_ascending": true,
            "restricted": false
          },
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: Create MediaAttribute - Success (201)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-07. No type-specific optional fields beyond the common name/label/description.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-attributes
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "name": "wc_test_media",
        "type": "MediaAttribute"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 201
      text: Created
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "id": "6a9f1bf92b6fd055ffb7c7e5",
            "name": "wc_test_media",
            "label": "wc_test_media",
            "description": null,
            "status": "ACTIVE",
            "type": "MediaAttribute"
          },
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: Create FormulaAttribute - Account Limit Reached (422)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-07. Dev account capped at 2 formula attributes (already at limit). Request body is otherwise valid -- the create path for FormulaAttribute itself remains unconfirmed on a fresh account.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-attributes
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "name": "wc_test_formula",
        "type": "FormulaAttribute",
        "formula_str": "IF(price>0,\"has price\",\"no price\")"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 422
      text: Unprocessable Entity
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": [
            {
              "name": "ValidationError",
              "description": "This account reached the limit of 2 formula attributes"
            }
          ]
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: Create Attribute - Invalid Type (422, full enum revealed)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-07. The pydantic error message is an authoritative list of all 15 valid type tags the live API recognizes -- one more than the 14 in openapi_pimv3.json (HierarchyAttribute is undocumented in the spec).

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-attributes
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "name": "wc_test_badtype",
        "type": "NotARealType"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 422
      text: Unprocessable Entity
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": [
            {
              "name": "InputDTOValidationError",
              "description": "Input tag 'NotARealType' found using 'type' does not match any of the expected tags: 'TextAttribute', 'MultilineAttribute', 'BooleanAttribute', 'DateAttribute', 'DecimalAttribute', 'DropdownAttribute', 'FormulaAttribute', 'HierarchyAttribute', 'HtmlAttribute', 'IntAttribute', 'MediaAttribute', 'MediaGalleryAttribute', 'MultiSelectAttribute', 'UrlAttribute', 'CompletenessAttribute'"
            }
          ]
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: Create HierarchyAttribute - Unimplemented (500)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-07. HierarchyAttribute passes pydantic discriminator validation (it is a recognized type tag) but the create handler is not wired up -- do not build customer-facing docs around this type.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-attributes
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "name": "wc_test_hierarchy",
        "type": "HierarchyAttribute"
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 500
      text: Internal Server Error
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": [
            {
              "name": "ConfigurationError",
              "description": "There was an error processing your request. Please try again later"
            }
          ]
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: Create CompletenessAttribute - With Real References (500, Bug)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-08 (reproduced twice). CompletenessAttribute with an empty attributes array creates successfully (201), but providing real attribute references in the correct {id} object shape triggers a 500 -- a live bug blocking any real use of Completeness Attributes.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-attributes
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "name": "wc_test_completeness_real",
        "type": "CompletenessAttribute",
        "attributes": [{"id": "6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e1"}]
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 500
      text: Internal Server Error
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": [
            {
              "name": "ConfigurationError",
              "description": "There was an error processing your request. Please try again later"
            }
          ]
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
